r you  as well number 11. the champions every  beginning ending and sometimes even  midpoint in a mission features a  high quality fully voice acted cinematic  cutscene that serves to delve into each  of the champions in depths that were  never explored in the original game  now this is partially due to the fact  that the setup for age of calamity is  you know back in the day when all of the  champions were still  alive and breath of the wild is set in  the future after they've all been gone  for 100 years but  even so it feels like age of calamity  just gave them more development than  breath of the wild  even tried to here's an example of what  i mean if you tally up the entire  run time of all cutscenes in the game it  comes out to about 15 minutes shy of 2  hours however  as i am of the opinion that you should  never be blocked behind a paywall from  experiencing a game's  story because of this i'm only going to  count the original game's packaged  cutscenes and am not going to count the  paid dlc cutscenes towards breath of the  wild's total run time  age of calamity's cutscenes on the other  hand tally up to two and a half  hours now one might think at first  glance that there's really not that big  of a difference between the two  but keep in mind that breath of the  wild's run time includes all of the  present day cut scenes that take place  after all the champions were already  dead and  largely does not even include them so if  you only include the cutscenes featuring  the living champions of 100 years ago  showing their  living personalities and character  development that totals up to  about 31 minutes 31 minutes of character  development split between  four individuals versus age of  calamities two and a half  hours that heavily features the other  champions after beating both of these  games i definitely felt more connected  to each of the champions after watching  and hearing them for hours in age of  calamity  and yes even bird boy number 10 the  voice acting i don't know what happened  and maybe it's just the actor and me  talking but it felt like the actors were  super on the ball this time around  not trying to say they were bad  necessarily in the original game but  say what you will about the english  voices one thing we can all agree on is  the fact that not only did each of them  get  better with some of them reprising their  roles in completely different ways such  as impulse voice actress returning to  voice impa in a completely different  much more youthful fashion but there  were also some new additions that just  knocked our socks off  how the great calamity gunman  selected me this  cannot be my destiny it cannot be  9. the enemy speaking of new editions  one of the biggest changes to the story  of breath of the wild that age of  calamity introduced was the character  known as  astor pastor i mean astor for those who  don't know is a ganon worshiping prophet  who leads the yiga clan into combat  against the princess and her heroes and  is revealed to be the reason behind  their hostility at least in this version  of the story  the thing is i think the story needed  someone like him to pose as the villain  breath of the wild's main villain was  calamity gannon who was more of a  malicious being or  presence than an actual character it was  part of what made the game feel  somewhat emptier than the zelda games of  the past which have largely all featured  specific  villainous characters that link must  defeat namely one that you may have  heard of once or twice that goes by the  name of  ganondorf anyway astor provided age of  calamity story with an actual evil  presence that you can put a face to  every time you heard him laugh evilly or  insult coco or vow to destroy the  princess was another spark being lit in  your hero heart and his rather  disturbing presumed death at the end of  the game leaves you feeling like he  finally got what he deserved  unlike breath of the wild when defeating  ganon just kind of felt the same as  cleaning all the goop off that  godforsaken beach in mario sunshine  number 8 suga and the yiga clan  speaking of villains the entire yiga  clan in breath of the wild  always made very little sense to me  largely because their leader is such a  doofus  i mean he dances around stomping his  foot like a little baby and has a voice  like some sort of disney villain and is  so clumsy that he  actually defeats himself in the game why  and how exactly is this dreaded yiga  clan supposed to be intimidating or pose  any real threat at  all but age of calamity introduced a new  character that changed all of that  suga or as i like to call him big boy  this guy brought the clan the balance of  seriousness and  actual skill in contrast to koga's  otherwise  lack of those things suga was  intelligent powerful  driven and mysterious and served to  elevate the threat of the yiga clan in  the story and when he turns against  astor in the middle of the game it  creates  even more respect for him and his clan  by showing that they're not all just  bananas and fat jokes  they can actually change and evolve with  the story number 7  the music you guys music is a huge part  of a game's impact  no matter how you slice it in breath of  the wild the series veteran composer  koji kondo  actually stepped down from the role of  coming up with the game's music and was  replaced by a small team that included  manika katoaka  who previously composed the title screen  music for animal crossing new leaf now  there was never a  real concrete reason given for the  change of staffing but it can be assumed  that it was a decision made in favor of  breath of the wild's more  ambient focused soundtrack however  that's not to say there weren't any good  original tracks made for the game  each of the champions themes are amazing  and the theme for highway castle is  still on my playlist too this day but  even though breath of the wild had some  great music  the team for age of calamity used these  as stepping stones and not only wrote  some original new tracks but also  took all of these existing tracks from  breath of the wild and remade them  so expertly each of the champions themes  is the same tune but on steroids and  they use zelda's lullaby much more often  than the original game did whether  you're fighting  thousands of monsters or a main boss or  just watching the characters joke around  with each other  the music always seemed to fit  masterfully into the scene  number six time travel as you probably  know by now the entire game of age of  calamity takes place in an  alternate pass that was split when  terrico zelda's little eggbot  jumped back in time by a hundred years  in an effort to save everyone before the  calamity could kill  everyone if you think about it time  travel or manipulation is kind of a  staple in the zelda series oftentimes  making an appearance in many different  ways  for instance in ocarina of time  obviously there was time travel between  two different points in time creating  the major timeline split most fans are  very familiar with today  in majora's mask the entire game is  focused around going back in time  over and over again until you can save  the world  in wind waker hyrule castle is literally  paused in time until link can retrieve  the master sword  and skyward sword also heavily features  time travel to defeat demise with age of  calamity literally pulling the same kind  of time jump that's already been done in  skyward sword majora's mask and ocarina  of time and focusing on fixing the  events before they could get out of hand  it really did feel right at home in a  zelda narrative number five the story  shifting speaking of going back in time  when terrico first  front flipped into history and caused  some major changes to the past like the  activation of the shika towers  i and many others were pretty convinced  that nothing we were seeing at this  point was actually canon and to be  honest it's  either non-canon or takes place in a  different new timeline  which until expounded upon further makes  it only pseudo cannon since it doesn't  presently matter to the rest of the  timeline but that aside the changes that  the story writers made to the events of  100 years ago are  actually fantastic breath of the wild's  backstory is one of immense  tragedy and you feel it in the very  world around you  it's old weathered and forgotten but in  age of calamity  everybody feels alive and you get to  keep them that way when the first  sheikah tower is raised  eventually pura figures out how to  activate all of them which feels very  fitting for her character and gives her  more importance than she previously had  in breath of the wild the same goes for  robbie who with pura decoded tereko's  memories and was able to figure out  exactly when the calamity was going to  take place  well almost the champions getting to  meet each of their descendants and  followers was also  a very nice touch that i don't think  anybody saw coming i could go on but  i'll stop there  ultimately i feel like the shifts and  changes to breath of the wild's  backstory were  very welcome and deepened the connection  to the living world of hyrule  number 4 the masterful writing in the  same vein as the previous point  even though some things changed about  the story of 100 years ago  in pretty major ways they always  remained under the same spirit or  concept as the original story intended  for instance when zelda unlocks her  power originally as shown at the  beginning of this very game  it is in defense of link but after  everyone else has died in age of  calamity she unlocks her power in  defensive link  again but it's before everyone else died  the game is full of these parallels and  special moments that reference the  events of the original game while still  changing it up  very skillfully i was impressed number  three  the king i know i used the whole deeper  look into the lives of everyone who died  through cutscenes as a point earlier in  the video  but this one was way too important to  loop in with everybody else you see if  there's one truly hated character from  breath of the wild it's the king of  hyrule  due to his harsh conduct towards his  daughter zelda one would have to go  out of their way and read his  descriptions from the book of creating a  champion to ever know he  even truly loved her i see hatred  towards the king of hyrule  all the time and previously it was for  pretty good reason but in age of  calamity we actually get to see his  redemption  because not only is his life spared like  everyone else's but through this he  actually genuinely shows that he cares  very deeply for his daughter and even  apologizes to her for shirking his  responsibility as a father first and a  king second  even though it doesn't actually change  the horrible things he did to her when  she was growing up  such as being responsible for taking  tariko away in the first place  the fact that he is intent on giving his  life to save his precious daughter  and then they share this moment of  genuine tenderness towards one another  as a father and daughter should  just gave me chills because even though  he was mean to her and tried to force  her into discovering her powers in his  wife's absence  deep down she really was the most  important thing to him and all he was  trying to do was  save everyone since he knew the prophecy  stated that her powers needed to awaken  i mean look it even made master koga cry  number two the divine beasts even though  this isn't strictly a story element  it was a big enough and memorable enough  part of the gameplay which the story  depended on that i had to include it on  this list playing as each of the  incredibly powerful divine beasts makes  you wonder how ganon ever won  in the first place i mean yes it was by  taking control of them and not really  defeating them but that's besides the  point flying around as vam meadow  stomping around as varuta  ramming through enemies as vanoborus and  flinging lava everywhere as varudanya  were the elements of gameplay that  nobody knew they wanted but now can't  imagine the game without  it really makes you feel like they were  underused in the original game  especially with their dungeons each  being beatable in about 15 minutes or  less for a veteran zelda player and at  number one we have  link i'll just come right out and say it  i love what they did with link in this  game he has more emotion than what was  shown in breath of the wild and can  perform some pretty supernatural feats  and i'm not just talking about the  gameplay which probably shouldn't be  heralded as canon in the first place  in the original game we normally just  see the aftermath of what he's done but  don't ever really get to see him  in action except for when he's training  in the rain which is a cool scene don't  get me wrong  but it's not an actual fight in the  cutscenes for age of calamity though  he's shown  on screen to be essentially as fast or  faster than a guardian beam  can spar off against all four of the  blight cannons at once  can deflect this huge chunk of building  with one  arm and also leaps like 20 feet in the  air to finish climbing again with a jump  attack which i thought was an incredible  touch  he feels much more like the physical  boss that we know he is in breath of the  wild but never really got to see for  ourselves  and that pretty much sums up my list  what did you guys think is age of  calamity's story better than breath of  the wilds  just as good or worse let me know in the  comments below and also let me know what  your favorite part of the game was  thank you so much for watching it means  the world to me if you want to be my  favorite person ever please consider  dropping a like to get the video spread  around on youtube  and if you enjoy zelda games and would  like more nintendo content consider  subscribing to stick around for the next  one  huge thanks as always to my fabulous  supporters who make my day  every single day and i have some new  faces to introduce too  say hello to skyward gamer onyx plays  and just david who have all joined the  ranks of my elite  if you watching are interested in some  pretty awesome perks and helping the  next video come to life  feel free to check out that join button  below or follow the links in the  description to find out how also while  you're down there you'll find links to  my social media pages so come follow me  on instagram that's all i've got for  this one so as always i hope you have a  wonderful rest of your day  this is mason 10 abandoned signing out  [Music]  you

